{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1494921-healing-other-creatures-which-arcana","id":1494921,"title":"Healing other creatures, which Arcana?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-13T07:08:32-07:00","id":1494921,"title":"Healing other creatures, which Arcana?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused which Arcana is required to heal and achieve Life-like enhancing effect on the following:<ul><li>Vampires (I would assume Death alone suffices, maybe some Matter?)</li> <li>Changelings with organic features (just Life right?)</li> <li>Changelings with non-organic features such as rock bodies, flame instead of hair, etc (does this require Matter?)</li> <li>Prometheans (Life alone I would guess, but maybe does it need Death?)</li> <li>Mummies (same as Prometheans I think)</li> <li>Geists (just Life right?)</li> </ul>Those are my doubts, but if there are other peculiar supernatural creatures, please point them to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T11:07:03-07:00","id":1494929,"title":"","content":"I've heard somebody summarise the principles laid out in The Contagion Chronicle, and I think the general way is that something only needs extra Arcana if it makes logical sense that the functions being targeted would require that.<br /> <br /> So like, a vampire needs Death mixed into the Life because their body is simply a normal corpse being animated by dark forces and they have no innate biological functions, but a Changeling is pretty much a normal lifeform even if it has fanciful features added on, so Life alone suffices to heal it. I think Prometheans end up qualifying as a weird form of life, but still enough that extra Arcana aren't required.<br /> <br /> For the Arisen, I have a sense that it's supposed to be that they kind of simultaneously function as alive and undead in a way that permits healing magic to work on them as normal, at the same time as certain magic will interact with them as though they were corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T12:14:51-07:00","id":1494932,"title":"","content":"Death alone should suffice for vampires.<br /> The Miens of changelings aren't just aesthetical: A clockwork soldier animated by spinning gears would require Matter instead of Life.<br /> To be nit-picky: Geists require Death to heal their Corpus. Bound requires Life to heal their Health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T03:31:29-07:00","id":1494962,"title":"","content":"Just giving my 2 cents:<ul><li>Vampires: Just Death, since they are dead bodies walking around no other arcana is required.</li> <li>Changelings: Life.</li> <li>Changelings with non-organic features such as rock bodies, flame instead of hair, etc: Life would still work, since they are living beings. If I was the ST I would also allow Forces or Matter depending on the seeming.</li> <li>Prometheans: Life works, since they are living beings. Also, you can indirectly heal them with Forces by blasting them with electricity.</li> <li>Mummies: Mummies are considered both dead and alive, so Life and Death work both.</li> <li>Geists: Same as above, both Sin Eaters and a Geist who is inhabiting both are considered both dead and alive so Death and Life work both.</li> </ul><br /> Some others:<ul><li>Beast: Life, but to heal the Horror of the Beast when merged with the Horro you use Mind instead.</li> <li>Demon: While in cover they are healed as humans, so Life. In their Demonic form Life works too (they are still alive) but I would lso allow Matter to work on the mechanical part of these biomechanical monstrosities.</li> <li>Deviant: depends on the specific, I expect Life would work on most of them, and some might have other options depending on their Clade, like healing and Invasive with Matter or some Coactives with Forces or Spirit.</li> <li>Werewolf: Just Life.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T14:35:00-07:00","id":1494984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1494921-healing-other-creatures-which-arcana#post1494921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused which Arcana is required to heal and achieve Life-like enhancing effect on the following:<ul><li>Vampires (I would assume Death alone suffices, maybe some Matter?)</li> <li>Changelings with organic features (just Life right?)</li> <li>Changelings with non-organic features such as rock bodies, flame instead of hair, etc (does this require Matter?)</li> <li>Prometheans (Life alone I would guess, but maybe does it need Death?)</li> <li>Mummies (same as Prometheans I think)</li> <li>Geists (just Life right?)</li> </ul><br /> Those are my doubts, but if there are other peculiar supernatural creatures, please point them to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IMO<br /> Vampires - you only need death+life to specifically manipulate their vitae. To simply heal the vampire, just Death.<br /> Mummies - death or life work.<br /> Sin Eaters - live. Their Geist -death.Everything else on the list, just life I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T17:05:35-07:00","id":1494995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1494921-healing-other-creatures-which-arcana#post1494921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires (I would assume Death alone suffices, maybe some Matter?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Death. They're animated corpses. Matter doesn't enter into it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings with organic features (just Life right?)<br /> Changelings with non-organic features such as rock bodies, flame instead of hair, etc (does this require Matter?) </div> </div> </div>Life. There's no need to involve Matter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prometheans (Life alone I would guess, but maybe does it need Death? </div> </div> </div>Life. They're made from corpses and/or inanimate materials, but they're alive.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummies (same as Prometheans I think </div> </div> </div>Life, though their specific metaphysical state means you might also be able to manage it with Death.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geists (just Life right?) </div> </div> </div>Death. Sin-Eaters explicitly count as dead for the purposes of magic that differentiates between the living and the dead, and geists are ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T00:45:47-07:00","id":1495005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1494921-healing-other-creatures-which-arcana?p=1494995#post1494995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death. Sin-Eaters explicitly count as dead for the purposes of magic that differentiates between the living and the dead, and geists are ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But their bodies are still biologically alive, and so I posit that Life spells that reshapes living bodies are unaffected. Magic that specifically affects the living, however, (such as a Life Knowing spell to find all living beings within an area) has no effect, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}